From 06230b589766592ab43f5979d95729ad59b0be70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:39:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Defer a struct whose field type a macro defines
 (nuc-iron-doom ISSUE-006)

The layout pre-scan resolves every defstruct's field types before any macro
has expanded, so a written defstruct naming a struct that a macro produces
died with unknown type, in the same file or across an import. The pre-scan
now arms g-layout-defer for an unknown name, as it already did for an array
length that will not fold, and the struct is laid out at emission. A
misspelt type is still diagnosed there.

Test: doom-macro-struct-as-field-type, doom-deferred-field-typo.
Gate: 1672 pass, the same 4 suite-build AVR failures; bootstrap PASS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8hzrZakM3KWb32SpqKh
