+
+## DOOM-port fix: a macro-produced struct as a field type (2026-11-05)
+
+nuc-iron-doom ISSUE-006. `defrecord`-style macros produce structs, and a
+written `defstruct` naming one as a field type died in the layout pre-scan
+(Stage 15 W9 item 40) with `unknown type`, in the same file or from an
+imported one, because no macro has expanded when that pre-scan runs.
+
+- `g-layout-probe` is set while `extract-decl-name-and-type-layout` resolves
+  a field. `resolve-type-name` then answers an unknown name by arming
+  `g-layout-defer`, as an unfoldable array length already did, and
+  `defstruct-fill-layout` abandons the struct to `emit-defstruct`.
+- A misspelt field type is still diagnosed, at emission, with the same words.
+
+Test: `doom-macro-struct-as-field-type` in `tests/suite-doom.nuc`,
+`doom-deferred-field-typo` in `tests/manifest/diagnostics.edn`.
+
+Gate: 1672 pass, the same 4 suite-build AVR failures. Bootstrap PASS; the
+compiler's own IR is unchanged.
diff --git a/docs/macros.md b/docs/macros.md
index e9b700c..0e857e7 100644
--- a/docs/macros.md
+++ b/docs/macros.md
@@ -735,6 +735,10 @@ after the pre-scans have already walked the file:
   `defn` produced by an expansion on line 90 cannot be called from a `defn`
   written on line 10. Ordinary definition order applies to it, not the
   file-wide visibility the pre-scans give hand-written ones.
+- A struct a macro produces **may be a by-value field** of a written `defstruct`
+  that is emitted after the expansion: below the call, or in a file importing
+  this one. The layout pre-scan leaves that `defstruct` to its own emission
+  instead of refusing the field type.
 
 Otherwise a macro-produced definition is registered exactly like a written one.
 The expansion's protocols, struct names, `defn` signatures and values are
diff --git a/src/nucleusc.nuc b/src/nucleusc.nuc
index f96d734..1e3dfce 100644
--- a/src/nucleusc.nuc
+++ b/src/nucleusc.nuc
@@ -516,6 +516,10 @@
 ; frames down, inside `parse-type-from-node`, whose return type is a non-null
 ; `ref:Type`.
 (defvar g-layout-defer:i32 0)
+; Set while the layout prescan resolves a field's type. A type name a macro will
+; define is unknown until that macro's call is emitted (nuc-iron-doom ISSUE-006),
+; so the prescan defers the struct, through `g-layout-defer`, instead of dying.
+(defvar g-layout-probe:i32 0)
 ; Stage 15 W8 G-3: "this initializer may turn out not to be constant". Armed
 ; (save/set/restore) only around `defvar-const-init-ir`'s single classifying
 ; call into `defvar-init-ir`, where it turns that function's terminal
@@ -1838,7 +1842,9 @@
 ; by `defstruct-fill-layout` alone.
 (defn extract-decl-name-and-type-layout (node:?&Node out-name:&Symbol line:i32):?&Type
   (set! g-array-ok 3)
+  (set! g-layout-probe 1)
   (let (t:?&Type (extract-name-and-type node out-name line))
+    (set! g-layout-probe 0)
     (set! g-array-ok 0)
     (return t)))
 
diff --git a/src/union-registry.nuc b/src/union-registry.nuc
index dcee480..7edd040 100644
--- a/src/union-registry.nuc
+++ b/src/union-registry.nuc
@@ -528,6 +528,11 @@
   ; Stage 15 W1c: `unknown-type-message` (src/nucleusc.nuc) says plainly that
   ; the name is defined nowhere in the unit, and — for §2.7's reachability
   ; constraint, which W1 keeps — names the on-path file that does define it.
+  ; The layout prescan asks again at emission instead (`g-layout-probe`); the
+  ; placeholder is never laid out, because the deferred struct is abandoned.
+  (when (!= g-layout-probe 0)
+    (set! g-layout-defer 1)
+    (return ty-i32))
   (die-at line (unknown-type-message name))))
 
